From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller 9996: stop putting uninitialised memory in the AP MLD Config TLV

cntlr_gen_ap_mld_config() builds the TLV into a buffer from cmdu_reserve_tlv(),
which only returns a pointer and clears nothing (cmdu.c:637). The loop then
advances past four fields without writing them - AP_MLD_MAC_Addr (6), a 20-byte
reserved block, Affiliated_AP_MAC_Addr (6) and an 18-byte reserved block - so 50
bytes per MLD keep whatever the buffer previously held, and that goes out on the
wire.

The consequence is not the leak, it is the reload. The receiving agent decides
whether to reconfigure by hashing the entire TLV:

	if (update_sha256_hash(...AP_MLD_CONFIG..., a->ap_mld_cfg_sha256)) {
		mlo_process_ap_mld_config(...);
		a->reconfig_reason |= AGENT_RECONFIG_REASON_MLD_ID;
		timer_set(&a->reload_scheduler, RELOAD_TIMEOUT * 1000);
	} else
		"Skip AP MLD configuration TLV, no change"

With garbage in the gaps the hash differs on every generation, so the "no
change" branch is unreachable and the agent tears down and rebuilds its AP-MLD
on *every* AP MLD Config Request - whatever the request was actually for.

Measured on hardware 2026-08-01. A TID-to-Link policy was pushed to an agent
(patches 9993-9995); the policy itself arrived and was applied correctly, and
eight seconds later:

	hostapd: Could not read interface ap-mld-2 flags: No such device
	hostapd: Remove MLD interface ap-mld-2
	hostapd: Create MLD interface ap-mld-2 on phy phy0, radio mask: 6
	hostapd: Failed to create interface ap-mld-2: -23 (Too many open files
	         in system)

The neighbour backhauled through that AP-MLD lost its uplink and re-attached to
the controller instead. The mesh recovered on its own, and the file-descriptor
exhaustion was transient (416 of 812464 afterwards), but a steering policy that
rebuilds a radio is not a steering policy.

Zeroing is what the format asks for anyway: both MAC fields are preceded by
their *_Valid flag, which this generator sets to 0, and the remaining two blocks
are reserved. Done once after the reserve rather than at the four skip sites, so
that a field added later cannot reintroduce it.

This is not caused by the TTLM patches; they only made it visible. The TTLM
generator writes every byte it advances over.

diff -urN a/src/cntlr_tlv.c b/src/cntlr_tlv.c
--- a/src/cntlr_tlv.c	2026-08-01 21:51:02.627993211 +0200
+++ b/src/cntlr_tlv.c	2026-08-01 21:51:02.628072479 +0200
@@ -2538,6 +2538,44 @@
 	if (!t)
 		return -1;
 
+	/* Zero it first. cmdu_reserve_tlv() only hands back a pointer into the
+	 * CMDU buffer - it does not clear anything (cmdu.c:637) - and the loop
+	 * below advances past four fields without writing them:
+	 *
+	 *	len += 6;   AP_MLD_MAC_Addr
+	 *	len += 20;  reserved
+	 *	len += 6;   Affiliated_AP_MAC_Addr
+	 *	len += 18;  reserved
+	 *
+	 * That is 50 bytes per MLD of whatever the buffer happened to hold, and
+	 * it goes out on the wire.
+	 *
+	 * The cost is not cosmetic. handle_ap_mld_config_request() decides
+	 * whether to reconfigure by hashing the whole TLV
+	 * (update_sha256_hash -> AGENT_RECONFIG_REASON_MLD_ID -> reload_scheduler).
+	 * With garbage in the gaps the hash is different every time, so the
+	 * "no change, skip reconfiguration" branch can never be taken and the
+	 * agent rebuilds its AP-MLD on *every* AP MLD Config Request.
+	 *
+	 * Measured on hardware 2026-08-01: eight seconds after one such request
+	 * the agent logged
+	 *
+	 *	hostapd: Remove MLD interface ap-mld-2
+	 *	hostapd: Failed to create interface ap-mld-2: -23 (Too many open
+	 *	         files in system)
+	 *
+	 * and the neighbour that was backhauled through that AP-MLD lost its
+	 * uplink and had to re-attach elsewhere.
+	 *
+	 * Zeroing is also what the fields ask for: both MAC addresses are
+	 * preceded by their *_Valid flag, which this generator sets to 0, and
+	 * the other two blocks are reserved.
+	 *
+	 * Done once here rather than at the four skip sites so that a field
+	 * added later cannot reintroduce this.
+	 */
+	memset(t->data, 0, 1024);
+
 	tlv_data = (struct tlv_ap_mld_config *)t->data;
 
 	t->type = MAP_TLV_AP_MLD_CONFIG;
